{"entryId":"1606","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1606:1","sourceSha256":"e6c23ee903f15d8e3df0d7bf2033ced2bd9cb65b9b93d23650e8bc4d5c12aac0","englishSha256":"f5a0b8101c908831974193402a55d61513021bdf5ec8efa556d95042537cf439","citations":[{"id":"1606:1:citation-01","he":[135,159],"en":[228,254],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_Yeshanim_on_Yoma_57b.3"},"reference":"Tosafot Yeshanim on Yoma 57b:3","assessment":"Tosafot Yeshanim uses R. Chiyya and R. Shimon son of Rabbi as analogues for the terminological and chronology argument.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot Yeshanim on Yoma 57b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_Yeshanim_on_Yoma_57b.3"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-02","he":[191,243],"en":[350,362],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_57b.4"},"reference":"Menachot 57b:4","assessment":"The passage explicitly calls Rabbi Yoshiyah a student of Rabbi Yishmael, and immediately compares Rabbi Yonatan. It does not explicitly call both students there.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 57b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_57b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Menachot 57b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_57b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Menachot 57b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_57b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-03","he":[245,278],"en":[416,438],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_57b.12"},"reference":"Yoma 57b:12","assessment":"Direct Yoma dispute on mixing the sacrificial blood. The back and forth tests alternative attributions.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 57b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_57b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 57b:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_57b.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-04","he":[280,320],"en":[470,482],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_108a.10"},"reference":"Shabbat 108a:10","assessment":"The checked Bavli explicitly reads Yoshiyah and Natan. Heilprin proposes Yonatan and the source remains Natan here.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 108a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_108a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-05","he":[342,362],"en":[563,598],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_24a.11"},"reference":"Sotah 24a:11","assessment":"The direct Bavli pairs Yoshiyah and Yonatan on the scope of the sotah procedure. This is a separate locus from the proposed Shabbat reading.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 24a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_24a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 24a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_24a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-06","he":[406,442],"en":[664,692],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_22a.11"},"reference":"Berakhot 22a:11","assessment":"Berakhot directly supplies the three elders and the Yoshiyah mixed-species teaching, with Yehudah ben Beteira and Ilai in the same verse discussion.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 22a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_22a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Berakhot 22a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_22a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-07","he":[467,497],"en":[777,789],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_54a.7"},"reference":"Pesachim 54a:7","assessment":"Pesachim names Yoshiyah and Nechemyah speaking in their fathers’ names, with Yehudah then contributing on tongs.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 54a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_54a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-08","he":[670,700],"en":[1139,1162],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Midrash_Tehillim_36.3"},"reference":"Midrash Tehillim 36:3","assessment":"Direct Midrash Tehillim calls him the Great. The identification with the earlier tanna is the compiler’s tentative suggestion.","evidence":[{"reference":"Midrash Tehillim 36:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Midrash_Tehillim_36.3"},"witness":"OYW"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-09","he":[560,573],"en":[918,954],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Bamidbar_123.1"},"reference":"Sifrei Bamidbar 123:1","assessment":"Sifrei Bamidbar 123 in Chukat directly says Yoshiyah spoke before Yehudah ben Beteira about a blemish. The inherited Chazakat label has an identified comparison and can be corrected with the original recorded.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sifrei Bamidbar 123:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Bamidbar_123.1"},"witness":"Wikisource"}]},{"id":"1606:1:citation-10","he":[575,634],"en":[956,980],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_218.7"},"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 218:7","assessment":"Sifrei Devarim 218:7 names Zeira as transmitter to Yoshiyah and reports his presentation to Yehudah ben Beteira. The Sotah parallel has a first-person indirect object, and Jerusalem Sanhedrin also gives Zeira. Preserve the received כי זעירא, while rendering the exact compared source with the correction noted.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 218:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_218.7"},"witness":"Sefaria Vocalized Edition"},{"reference":"Sotah 25a:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_25a.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Sanhedrin 8:6:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Sanhedrin_8.6.2"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,8,9,7],"holds":[{"raw":"וצ\"ע כי נראה שהיה בזמן ריב\"ב","reason":"The late-tanna suggestion belongs to Tosafot Yeshanim. Heilprin questions it on the basis of Yehudah ben Beteira. The relative chronology and bearer require collation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot Yeshanim on Yoma 57b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_Yeshanim_on_Yoma_57b.3"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sifrei Bamidbar 123:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Bamidbar_123.1"},"witness":"Wikisource"}]},{"raw":"ר' יונתן ור' יאשיה תלמידי ר' ישמעאל","reason":"Menachot explicitly names Yoshiyah as a student. The corresponding assertion for Yonatan remains Heilprin’s report at this locus.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 57b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_57b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"נראה שצ\"ל ר' יונתן","reason":"The checked Shabbat witness reads Natan. Sotah attests the Yoshiyah/Yonatan pairing elsewhere. Keep the proposed Shabbat reading conjectural.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 108a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_108a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 24a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_24a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"אולי הוא הנ\"ל שהיה תנא","reason":"Keep Heilprin’s tentative identification of the Great with the earlier tanna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Midrash Tehillim 36:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Midrash_Tehillim_36.3"},"witness":"OYW"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Preserve Tosafot’s dating and Heilprin’s objection, Shabbat’s Natan and the proposed Yonatan. The exact comparison restores Chukat and Zeira’s first-person transmission. The received labels חזקת and כי זעירא remain in the Hebrew.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 57b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_57b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Tosafot Yeshanim on Yoma 57b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_Yeshanim_on_Yoma_57b.3"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Menachot 57b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_57b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Menachot 57b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_57b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Menachot 57b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_57b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 57b:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_57b.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 108a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_108a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 24a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_24a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 24a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_24a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Berakhot 22a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_22a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Berakhot 22a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_22a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 54a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_54a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sifrei Bamidbar 123:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Bamidbar_123.1"},"witness":"Wikisource"},{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 218:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_218